    "Imported from a single tls.peet.ws capture. Extension order is fixed to that sample, not a browser's complete randomized ordering policy.",
    "IP addresses, capture metadata, request header values, SNI, randoms, session IDs, key material and ECH ciphertext were removed; dynamic TLS values are generated per connection.",
    "GREASE extension bodies follow uTLS's BoringSSL behavior: first empty, second one zero byte; the capture does not expose their lengths.",
    "This is an experimental Chrome/152 capture profile, not a claim of complete Chrome 152 handshake or connection behavior support.",
    "Extension 51764 (0xca34) is TLS Trust Anchor IDs trust_anchors. This profile explicitly replays its captured advertisement, without implementing certificate selection or retry semantics.",
    "Signature algorithms 0x0904, 0x0905 and 0x0906 are advertised but not implemented by uTLS v1.8.2; negotiation of these algorithms fails."
